\ A helper whose own body cannot compile. It reads a binding of an untyped input, and the callers
\ pass both a number and a quotation, so nothing proves the read pushes one value. The helper's
\ read compiles to that body, so the build refuses the enclosing word instead of trapping at runtime.

pass-through: ( a -- a ) [
  kept: swap ;
  get-kept: [ kept ] ;
  get-kept
] ;

7 pass-through .
[ 8 ] pass-through .
